#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# struve_l

#% text
# `struve_l(nu, z)` gives the modified Struve function `L_nu(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `L_nu(z)` is `-im*exp(-im*nu*pi/2)*H_nu(im*z)` (DLMF 11.2.2), the series of `(z/2)^(2k + nu + 1)/(gamma(k + 3/2)*gamma(k + nu + 3/2))`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values; symbolic arguments stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
struve_l(0, 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.7102431859378909

#% cell
struve_l(1, 2.5)
#% output
#= 1.9880307722359416

#% cell
struve_l(0.5, 2.0)
#% output
#= 1.558402036629881

#% cell
n(struve_l(0, 1), 30)
#% output
#= 0.7102431859378908887385266778116507

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# For large `x`, `L_0(x)` and `I_0(x)` agree to all but a tiny relative difference:

#% cell
(struve_l(0, 20.0) - bessel_i(0, 20.0))/bessel_i(0, 20.0)
#% output
#= -7.326388656826871e-10


#% text
# Half-integer orders are elementary:

#% cell
struve_l(1/2, x)
#% output
#= -2^(1/2)/(pi^(1/2)*x^(1/2)) + cosh(x)*2^(1/2)/(pi^(1/2)*x^(1/2))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `struve_h`, `bessel_i`
